{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/651473-decapitation-2ed","id":651473,"title":"Decapitation [2ed]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-04T10:45:34-07:00","id":651473,"title":"Decapitation [2ed]","content":"Hi all,<br /> I have a question about decapitation during a combat: In the corebook in order to hit the head there is a -3 penality to apply to the dice pool. Usually to an arm or a leg wrack action, the required successes in this roll are equal to the Stamina amount (or size for the head). Is this rule the same to cut the head with a sword or is there another specific mechanic that I didn't find? If it is the same, what's the difference between a shotguns hit and a head cut? Or better, between stun effect and head cutting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T11:18:52-07:00","id":651514,"title":"","content":"The arm and leg wrack tilts are only temporary, representing short-term damage. Actually removing the arm or leg requires the same amount of aggravated damage. There is no rule for decapatation (besides ST fiat), but it wouldn't be unreasonable to rule that a hit that deals aggravated damage &gt; the target's stamina on a targeted attack to the head removes or destroys it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 09-04-2015, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T12:31:58-07:00","id":651628,"title":"","content":"But if you can do it, so can others. Would you be okey with your character being removed from the game in a single roll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T13:01:38-07:00","id":651727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/651473-decapitation-2ed?p=651628#post651628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you can do it, so can others. Would you be okey with your character being removed from the game in a single roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of the time, if you're taking more aggravated damage than your stamina in a single hit that was made at a -3 penalty, you're probably dead anyway. I don't use that rule myself, but like I said, I wouldn't find it unreasonable for an ST to rule that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T13:39:24-07:00","id":651742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/651473-decapitation-2ed?p=651628#post651628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you can do it, so can others. Would you be okey with your character being removed from the game in a single roll?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that it's a possible action so it could happen also to a PC. A PC should be smart and don't put himself in dangerous situation like this. <br /> Anyway there is yet the mechanics of the impalement so, in a single roll, a character could be removed from the game anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-04T14:00:31-07:00","id":651766,"title":"","content":"My character was attacking a ghoul and going after their arm in urshul, the near-wolf form. She was dual wielding pistols loaded with silver bullets, I figured taking one out would deal with it. My character's a big humanitarian so the damage was aggravated and I got an obscene roll, I think with six successes, which was big considering my character's otherwise subpar combat ability. So we decided most of her shoulder and a good portion of her torso came with the arm.<br /> <br /> We never found the gun.<br /> <br /> It does say Tilts done with aggravated damage cause permanent disability, not necessarily destruction. If you wanted you could decide a called shot to the head doing aggravated damage would, instead of Stun, cause some sort of severely disabling Tilt until the vampire healed it. If you didn't want to just lop off the head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T14:39:19-07:00","id":653038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/651473-decapitation-2ed?p=651628#post651628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if you can do it, so can others. Would you be okey with your character being removed from the game in a single roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>If your players are using one shot decapitation as the solution to everything, introduce this guy.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://www.wired.com/images_blogs/underwire/2013/09/SH02.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T15:42:59-07:00","id":653100,"title":"","content":"It isn't realistic to decapitate someone during combat. A shotgun to the face won't do it. You might have a shot if you aimed at the back of the neck. Typically, the effects look much more gruesome that a decapitation. Melee weapons are even worse unless the person is held in place. You could get close enough in either case that a person would be dead as a doornail (or Dickens). It is like cutting through a weapon, virtually impossible. Decapitation, proper, is better represented as a coup de grace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T16:03:12-07:00","id":653121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/651473-decapitation-2ed?p=653100#post653100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't realistic to decapitate someone during combat. A shotgun to the face won't do it. You might have a shot if you aimed at the back of the neck. Typically, the effects look much more gruesome that a decapitation. Melee weapons are even worse unless the person is held in place. You could get close enough in either case that a person would be dead as a doornail (or Dickens). It is like cutting through a weapon, virtually impossible. Decapitation, proper, is better represented as a coup de grace.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's how I do it. Only allowed on a Killing Blow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}